  "details": "Before you begin, make sure AFK detection is enabled.\nTested on the Open Beta, but also occurs on Live.\nRepro steps:\n1.) Be in FBT\n2.) Calibrate in your usual SDK3 avatar\n3.) Now switch into an SDK2 avatar\n4.) While your avatar is loading, quickly bring up your SteamVR menu\n5.) Close menu after your avatar finishes loading\nExpected result: VRChat should now think you are in just 3 pt tracking and your avatar should continue to function as normal.\nActual result: All IK on your avatar is broken. Locally, you move like you're in desktop, but remotely for others you appear to just be sliding around.\nThis bug was previously thought to be inconsistent but after some testing, it turns out AFK Detection has a part in this bug and can mess with your IK with it's animation as you're coming out of the SteamVR menu.\nVideo: https://files.catbox.moe/at40n6.mp4",
